=== ablation [X1]: own-array defineAt reverts to ordinary indexed assignment (the exact H7 operation) ===
packages/kernel/src/own-array.ts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)
    193 tests, 10 failing -> REJECTED by 10 case(s):
      - a coherent array whose prototype observation installs an indexed accessor binds its own value
      - a bound getter that installs Array.prototype["0"] still reserves the exact available prefix
      - the same trap at every reserved index cannot shorten a larger batch either
      - an inherited setter at the next mailbox index cannot make an accepted Event go unretained
      - a creation whose payload traps the first mailbox index still binds its initial Event
      - inspect and visibleExecutions report the same facts with the accessor live as without it
      - a refusal recorded under the accessor is still retained evidence a later read reports
      - the retained structure and the canonical bytes are exactly the one value observed
      - the index the accessor picks is not special: position zero and a nested array behave the same
      - an inherited accessor at the indices the serializer writes cannot choose the bytes

